// The clerk's decisions (vault designs/policy-language-draft-2026-11-08.md §15–§16): asked by nets/clerk.net.

// How an agent's turn end is taken when it waits on nothing coordd knows of: accepted (it waits for its wake),
// nudged ("do that next") or, past the cap, told to the owner. The net gives the clerk's reading of the turn (state:
// Done, Next, Blocked, Waiting), the nudges in a row so far (nudged) and the length of what it wrote (said). Each
// case is said outright (9 Nov: the cap escalated only because "nudge > escalate" ranked the unnamed accept last).
Decision end-of-turn
  Options accept | nudge | escalate
// Only a turn that names its own next step and stops (Next) is nudged or told; any other is accepted.
Only for end-of-turn When call.state != "Next":
  option == "accept"
// A turn whose text came out empty is accepted: there is nothing it could have said it would do next.
Only for end-of-turn When call.said == 0:
  option == "accept"
// Past three nudges in a row there is no fourth: the owner is told instead.
Only for end-of-turn When call.nudged >= 3:
  option != "nudge"
Prefer for end-of-turn When call.state == "Next" and call.nudged >= 3:
  option == "escalate" > option == "accept"
// Below the cap, a Next is nudged.
Prefer for end-of-turn When call.state == "Next":
  option == "nudge" > option == "escalate" > option == "accept"

// Whether the owner's message gets a spell check first: not a short reply ("yes", "1 yes 2 no").
Decision needs-spellcheck
  Options yes | no
Prefer for needs-spellcheck When call.length < 16:
  option == "no"
Prefer for needs-spellcheck:
  option == "yes"
